<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><base href="../"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Ambient patch review · El’s Invitation</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="adventure/world.css"><style>
main{max-width:1536px;padding-bottom:60px}.intro,.notes{max-width:920px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted)}.review-note{padding:18px 22px;background:#eee2c6;border:1px solid #c6ab75;border-radius:8px;max-width:920px;line-height:1.8}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin:24px 0}.controls select{padding:10px;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px}.controls button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#42634d;color:#fff8e9}.scene{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;aspect-ratio:1.5;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:#e2d5b5}.patch-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;margin:24px 0}.patch-card{padding:18px;background:#f1e7d1;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;min-width:0}.patch-card h3{margin:0 0 14px}.patch-card p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.crop-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px}.crop-pair figure{margin:0;min-width:0}.crop-pair canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:200px;object-fit:contain;background:#dbcfb5;border-radius:5px}.crop-pair figcaption{font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--muted)}#motionStatus{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.notes{font-size:13px}.notes h2{font-size:22px;color:var(--ink)}@media(max-width:750px){.patch-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.world-header{flex-wrap:wrap}.crop-pair canvas{height:170px}}
</style></head><body><header class="world-header"><a class="brand" href="adventure/"><span class="brand-sun">☀</span><span><small>EL’S INVITATION · REVISED STUDY</small><strong>Ambient patch review</strong></span></a><a href="adventure/">Return to your adventure →</a></header><main><span class="eyebrow">COHERENT RIVERSIDE SECTION · NOW IN THE ADVENTURE</span><h1>A living section of the riverside</h1><p class="intro">The latest Kling 4.0 take animates this full riverside crop together: reeds across the upper, middle and lower banks, plus water highlights and ripples around the pier. The five-second, 720p job cost 50 credits. This approved take is now enabled in the live Riverside Quarter, with reduced-motion support.</p><section id="riverside-section"><h2>Kling 4.0 · reeds and water together</h2><p class="notes">Play the full section, switch to the original art, or inspect it at its exact map position. The earlier reed-only salvage is available in the take selector for comparison. Matching endpoint images were supplied, but the generated endpoints still differ slightly; inspect the loop boundary.</p><div class="controls"><label>Take <select id="sectionTake"><option value="latest">Latest · Kling 4.0 full section</option><option value="earlier">Earlier · Kling 3.0 reed salvage</option></select></label><button id="sectionPlay" aria-pressed="false">Play section</button><button id="sectionOriginal" aria-pressed="false">Compare original</button><button id="sectionMask" aria-pressed="false">Show replacement mask</button><button id="sectionView" aria-pressed="false">Show whole map</button></div><p id="sectionStatus" role="status">Loading riverside section…</p><canvas id="sectionScene" class="scene" width="480" height="672" style="aspect-ratio:480/672;max-width:600px" aria-label="Full coherent riverside animation with moving reeds and water, fixed pier and original comparison"></canvas><p class="notes">The map preview registers the clip against stationary land, feathers the crop perimeter and preserves original pier/post pixels. Complete moving reeds and their revealed background are replaced together. The latest take has no loop crossfade or retiming applied. Review the untouched output below to distinguish generated motion from compositing.</p><details><summary>Untouched full-section output, boundaries and checks</summary><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-source-v3.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;max-width:480px" aria-label="Untouched full-section Kling 4.0 animation"></video><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-v3.json">Generation provenance · 50 credits</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-v3-review.json">Frame and registration checks</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-v3-prompt.txt">Exact prompt</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-mask-v3.png">Latest compositing mask</a></p><p>The earlier salvage mask protected the flashing corner in the Kling 3.0 footage. The latest full-section output uses a broader mask to retain the new reed and water motion. The approved latest clip is enabled in the Riverside Quarter; the earlier experiments remain study-only.</p></details><video id="sectionVideo" src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-section-registered-v3.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="auto" style="display:none"></video></section><section id="next-sections"><h2>Courtyard and sanctuary · now animated</h2><p class="notes">Both coherent sections are now in the adventure. This batch used exactly 100 credits, 50 per clip. The previews below use the same slower playback rates as the game, giving each area a distinct loop period and starting offset. The original matching keyframes and untouched outputs are retained for comparison; no loop crossfade is applied.</p><div class="crop-pair"><figure><figcaption>Courtyard canal gardens · 5.8-second effective loop</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/courtyard-canals-registered-v1.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/courtyard-canals-input-v1.png" data-ambient-preview-rate="0.87" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Animated courtyard canal gardens"></video><p class="notes">Visible canal ripple and reed motion; small endpoint mismatch; cropped upper temple decorations preserved from static map.</p><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/courtyard-canals-source-v1.mp4">Untouched output</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/courtyard-canals-review-v1.json">Frame checks</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/courtyard-canals-input-v1.png">Input image</a></p></figure><figure><figcaption>Sanctuary altar and lamps · 6.9-second effective loop</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/sanctuary-altar-registered-v1.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/sanctuary-altar-input-v1.png" data-ambient-preview-rate="0.73" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Animated sanctuary altar and lamps"></video><p class="notes">Visible flames, banners, plant leaves and bowl ripples; small endpoint mismatch; fixed architecture remains aligned.</p><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/sanctuary-altar-source-v1.mp4">Untouched output</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/sanctuary-altar-review-v1.json">Frame checks</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/sanctuary-altar-input-v1.png">Input image</a></p></figure></div><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/prepared.json">Generation provenance, crop coordinates and timing</a></p></section><section id="cedar-rig"><h2>New approach - one cedar with layered branches</h2><p class="notes">A standalone pilot with a fixed trunk and three reusable foliage pieces. Inspect the animation enlarged or at map scale, pause and scrub its 120 frames, and view the separate parts. This uses a new cutout tree based on the grove style; it has not been composited into the live map.</p><p><a href="adventure/cedar-rig-study.php">Open the one-tree layer study →</a></p></section><section id="cedar-sustained"><h2>Cedar grove - rejected trim, reference only</h2><p class="notes">Rejected after visual review. Trimming the quiet frames and slowing playback did not fix the unnatural tree bending and changing foliage shapes in the generated take. This clip is retained only as a reference, not a proposed replacement. No new generation credits were spent on the trim. The live grove was not changed.</p><div class="controls"><label>Speed <select id="cedarSustainedSpeed"><option value=".3">30% - slower</option><option value=".4" selected>40% - default</option><option value=".5">50% - brisker</option></select></label><button id="cedarSustainedPlay" aria-pressed="false">Play rejected reference</button><button id="cedarSustainedOriginal" aria-pressed="false">Compare original map</button></div><video id="cedarSustainedVideo" src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-active-loop-v6.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;max-width:700px;height:auto" aria-label="Active inner cycle of the cedar grove at a slower playback speed"></video><p id="cedarSustainedStatus" role="status">Loading new take...</p><h3>At its original map position</h3><p class="notes">The crop is aligned to stationary ground and masked at the existing grove boundary. Only the grove region is replaced; the surrounding map stays static. The loop uses similar branch poses at its join; it has a small remaining mismatch rather than an added dissolve.</p><canvas id="cedarSustainedMap" class="scene" width="1536" height="1024" aria-label="Slower active cedar loop composited at original map scale"></canvas><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-active-loop-v6.json">Trim and loop checks</a> &middot; <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-source-v5.mp4">Untouched Kling output</a> &middot; <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-sustained-v5.json">Generation record</a> &middot; <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-sustained-wind-v5-prompt.txt">Prompt</a> &middot; <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-v5-activity-comparison.json">Motion across the whole clip</a></p></section><section id="cedar-strengths"><h2>Cedar breeze · earlier takes for reference</h2><p class="notes">The continuous-motion experiment was rejected: its local image warping bends and ripples the illustration instead of producing natural branch sway. Those clips have been withdrawn from this comparison. The earlier versions below are retained only for reference; they still have the single-gust / long-pause problem and are not approved replacements. The live game is unchanged. A new whole-section Kling take is available immediately above; it still has quiet intervals near the loop ends.</p><div class="controls"><button id="cedarStrengthPlay">Play / restart all three</button><button id="cedarStrengthPause">Pause all three</button></div><div class="cedar-strength-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,320px),1fr));gap:18px"><figure style="margin:0;min-width:0"><figcaption>Light breeze · up to 4 pixels at source size</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-light-v3.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" data-cedar-strength="light" data-ambient-preview-rate=".91" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Cedar light breeze comparison"></video><p><button data-cedar-toggle="light" data-label="light breeze" aria-pressed="false">Play light breeze</button></p></figure><figure style="margin:0;min-width:0"><figcaption>Clear breeze · up to 7 pixels at source size</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-medium-v3.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" data-cedar-strength="medium" data-ambient-preview-rate=".91" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Cedar clear breeze comparison"></video><p><button data-cedar-toggle="medium" data-label="clear breeze" aria-pressed="false">Play clear breeze</button></p></figure><figure style="margin:0;min-width:0"><figcaption>Strong breeze · up to 10 pixels at source size</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-strong-v3.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" data-cedar-strength="strong" data-ambient-preview-rate=".91" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Cedar strong breeze comparison"></video><p><button data-cedar-toggle="strong" data-label="strong breeze" aria-pressed="false">Play strong breeze</button></p></figure></div><h3>Check it at map scale</h3><p class="notes">Only the selected cedar variation plays in this map preview. The rest of the map is shown as static context.</p><div class="controls"><label>Map preview <select id="cedarStrengthChoice"><option value="light">Light breeze · 4 pixels</option><option value="medium" selected>Clear breeze · 7 pixels</option><option value="strong">Strong breeze · 10 pixels</option></select></label><button id="cedarStrengthOriginal" aria-pressed="false">Compare original</button></div><p id="cedarStrengthStatus" role="status">Loading comparisons…</p><canvas id="cedarStrengthMap" class="scene" width="1536" height="1024" aria-label="Selected cedar breeze at its original map position and scale"></canvas><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-strength-study-v3.json">Motion limits and trunk checks</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-strength-motion-region-v3.png">Branch motion region</a></p></section><section id="grove-temple"><h2>New · restrained cedar and temple court</h2><p class="notes">Both approved Kling 4.0 jobs are complete, submitted at 50 credits each within the 100-credit cap. The temple take is now in the adventure. The cedar retry still distorted the trees, so the live cedar instead uses a locally restrained version: the original drawing follows a smoothed motion guide from Kling, limited to two pixels. No generated twig textures are copied, and this processing used no additional credits.</p><div class="crop-pair"><figure><figcaption>Live cedar · original artwork with restrained motion · 5.5-second period</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-restrained-v2.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" data-ambient-preview-rate=".91" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Restrained cedar motion preserving the original drawing"></video><p class="notes">Complete foliage motion stays within a two-pixel displacement. Cropped palms and market objects remain fixed. Endpoint drift is corrected locally; the first and last frames are exactly original before encoding.</p><details><summary>Compare raw cedar generations</summary><p class="notes">The new raw retry below still changes the foliage shapes and adds twig details. It is a motion guide only, not the live artwork.</p><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-source-v2.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-input-v1.png" data-ambient-preview-rate=".91" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto" aria-label="Raw cedar retry with unwanted foliage deformation"></video><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-source-v1.mp4">Previous cedar take</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-restrained-v2.json">Local motion method and limits</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/cedar-grove-review-v2.json">Raw retry measurements</a></p></details></figure><figure><figcaption>Live temple · banners and palm leaves · 6.4-second period</figcaption><video src="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/temple-court-registered-v2.mp4" poster="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/temple-court-input-v1.png" data-ambient-preview-rate=".79" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:650px;object-fit:contain" aria-label="Animated temple court with moving banners and palm leaves"></video><p class="notes">Architecture and statues remain aligned. The empty braziers stay empty. The partial terrace and overlap with the canal are excluded from the replacement mask. Small endpoint differences remain in the raw temple loop.</p><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/temple-court-source-v2.mp4">Untouched temple output</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/temple-court-review-v2.json">Frame checks</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/temple-court-mask-v2.png">Compositing mask</a></p></figure></div><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-sections/grove-temple-retry-v2.json">Batch prompts, source jobs and provenance</a></p></section><details><summary>Earlier pilots and compositing experiments</summary><section id="water-v2"><h2>Kling 4.0 · isolated water test</h2><p class="intro">The second pilot uses matching first and last frames and a tight crop containing only water. Ripples visibly shift in this take. The five-second, 720p job cost 50 credits. Review the untouched loop below, then play it while comparing the marked patch in the original map.</p><div class="crop-pair"><figure><figcaption>Exact input · enlarged from a 62×70 map region</figcaption><img src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-v2-input.png" width="496" height="560" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-width:496px" alt="Turquoise illustrated water with ripple highlights"></figure><figure><figcaption>Untouched Kling 4.0 output · press play to review the loop</figcaption><video id="waterV2Video" src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-source-v2.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" style="width:100%;max-width:496px" aria-label="Five-second Kling 4 water loop"></video></figure></div><p class="notes">The small source crop isolates the water behavior but limits detail; enlargement does not add resolution. The map comparison restores its exact original size and feathers the water patch boundary. No extra motion, loop crossfade or retiming is applied. This pilot is not enabled in the adventure.</p><div class="controls"><button id="waterV2Toggle" aria-pressed="true">Show original water</button><button id="waterV2Focus" aria-pressed="false">Inspect pier context</button></div><canvas id="waterV2Scene" class="scene" width="1536" height="1024" aria-label="Isolated water pilot at its exact map position; pale outline marks the small test area"></canvas><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/pilot-v2.json">Settings and provenance</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/water-v2-prompt.txt">Exact prompt</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/review-v2.json">Frame measurements</a></p></section><section id="generated-pilot"><h2>Kling water pilot · motion too subtle</h2><p class="intro">One five-second Kling 3.0 take was generated for 45 credits. The scenery stayed aligned, but the water barely moves. This take is here for review and is not enabled in the adventure.</p><div class="controls"><button id="generatedToggle" aria-pressed="false">Play masked take</button><button id="generatedFocus" aria-pressed="false">Inspect pier crop</button></div><p id="generatedStatus" role="status">Loading pilot…</p><canvas id="generatedScene" class="scene" width="1536" height="1024" aria-label="Actual Kling water take masked onto the unchanged Riverside map"></canvas><details><summary>Raw take, preparation and checks</summary><p>The preview registers each frame to the input scenery, then admits it only through the reviewed water mask. Before video encoding, compositing changed zero pixels outside that mask. An eight-frame end blend closes the loop. Neither step creates the flowing water this take lacks.</p><video id="generatedWater" src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-registered-v1.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="auto" controls style="max-width:100%;max-height:560px"></video><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-source-v1.mp4">Untouched Kling output</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/review.json">Registration and mask measurements</a></p></details></section><h2>Earlier ripple and mask study</h2><div class="controls"><label>Map <select id="sceneChoice"><option value="courtyard">The First Courtyard</option><option value="riverside">The Riverside Quarter</option></select></label><button id="motionToggle" aria-pressed="true">Water preview on</button><button id="maskToggle" aria-pressed="false">Show exact water mask</button><button id="boundsToggle" aria-pressed="false">Show context rectangles</button><button id="resetZoom">Whole map</button></div><p id="motionStatus" role="status"></p><canvas id="scene" class="scene" width="1536" height="1024" aria-label="Water animation and protected-scenery study"></canvas><div id="patchList" class="patch-list"></div>
<section class="notes"><h2>What changed</h2><p>The old row-by-row image warping is removed. This preview adds moving ripple strokes inside a stationary water mask; it does not translate or bend any source pixels. The mask leaves a four-pixel guard band around detected water boundaries, plus a feathered context edge. It is a compositing test, not a generated video or final approval of the animation style.</p><h2>Moving objects need a different preparation</h2><p>A palm or flag needs its entire moving silhouette isolated, with room for its full motion. The original silhouette must be removed from the underlying static art, revealing a reconstructed background. Otherwise the old and moving outlines can double up. Anchor points and foreground occlusion also need checking. The old tree strips, partial awnings and narrow banner crops are not suitable generation inputs.</p><h2>Prepared five-second water pilot</h2><p>The first pilot uses a 480×672 context crop around the pier, with the exact reviewed water mask exported alongside it. Identical input images were used as first and last frames. The approved single job is complete; see the actual masked take above.</p><div class="crop-pair"><figure><figcaption>Prepared context input</figcaption><img src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-input-v1.png" width="480" height="672" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-width:300px" alt="Riverside animation input, including the fixed pier and banks"></figure><figure><figcaption>Compositing mask · white may change</figcaption><img src="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/riverside-water-mask-v1.png" width="480" height="672" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-width:300px" alt="Exact grayscale water mask protecting the pier, banks and plants"></figure></div><p><a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/water-pilot-prompt.txt">Exact video prompt</a> · <a href="adventure/assets/ambient-pilot/pilot.json">Pilot settings and approval status</a></p><h2>Before expanding the batch</h2><p>Begin with one padded water crop and a fixed camera. Composite the result only through the reviewed water mask; a prompt asking for fixed scenery is not a sufficient safeguard. Check the clip’s registration, normal-size motion, seam and loop before expanding the batch. Give approved clips distinct loop lengths and phase offsets. The first pilot used its approved 45 credits; the second Kling 4.0 pilot used a separately approved 50 credits. No additional jobs have been submitted.</p><p>The live adventure now uses the approved Kling 4.0 riverside section; these earlier experiments remain study-only. Reduced-motion settings also default this preview to off; you can explicitly enable it here.</p></section></details></main><script src="adventure/background-motion.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/background-motion.js')?>"></script><script>
'use strict';
const canvas=document.getElementById('scene'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d'),engine=DFGBackgroundMotion.create(),maps={courtyard:'adventure/assets/sumerian-overworld-v1.png',riverside:'adventure/assets/riverside-quarter-v1.webp'},loaded={};
let zone='courtyard',enabled=!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches,showMask=false,bounds=false,focus=null;
function sync(){const b=document.getElementById('motionToggle');b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(enabled));b.textContent=enabled?'Water preview on':'Water preview off';document.getElementById('motionStatus').textContent=showMask?'Pink = editable water. Everything outside that mask remains untouched.':enabled?'Ripple preview only · fixed source image · independent loop timing':'Static comparison of this earlier procedural study.';}
function list(){const root=document.getElementById('patchList');root.replaceChildren();for(const p of DFGBackgroundMotion.patches[zone]){const card=document.createElement('article');card.className='patch-card';const heading=document.createElement('h3');heading.textContent=p.name;const pair=document.createElement('div');pair.className='crop-pair';for(const mask of [false,true]){const f=document.createElement('figure'),caption=document.createElement('figcaption'),c=document.createElement('canvas');caption.textContent=mask?'Editable mask · pink only':'Source context · stationary';c.width=p.box[2];c.height=p.box[3];const cc=c.getContext('2d');cc.drawImage(engine.source(loaded[zone],p),0,0);if(mask){cc.globalAlpha=.75;cc.drawImage(engine.mask(loaded[zone],p),0,0);}f.append(caption,c);pair.append(f);}const note=document.createElement('p');note.textContent=`${p.seconds.toFixed(1)} second candidate period · phase ${Math.round(p.phase*100)}% · context ${p.box.join(', ')}. Nearby objects are excluded from the editable mask.`;const button=document.createElement('button');button.textContent='Focus this patch';button.addEventListener('click',()=>{focus=p;canvas.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});});card.append(heading,pair,note,button);root.append(card);}}
document.getElementById('motionToggle').addEventListener('click',()=>{enabled=!enabled;sync();});document.getElementById('maskToggle').addEventListener('click',e=>{showMask=!showMask;e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(showMask));sync();});document.getElementById('boundsToggle').addEventListener('click',e=>{bounds=!bounds;e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(bounds));});document.getElementById('resetZoom').addEventListener('click',()=>focus=null);document.getElementById('sceneChoice').addEventListener('change',e=>{zone=e.target.value;focus=null;list();});
function frame(time){requestAnimationFrame(frame);const bg=loaded[zone];if(!bg)return;ctx.clearRect(0,0,1536,1024);ctx.fillStyle='#e4d8bc';ctx.fillRect(0,0,1536,1024);ctx.save();if(focus){const [x,y,w,h]=focus.box,pad=30,scale=Math.min(1536/(w+pad*2),1024/(h+pad*2));ctx.translate(768-(x+w/2)*scale,512-(y+h/2)*scale);ctx.scale(scale,scale);ctx.beginPath();ctx.rect(x-pad,y-pad,w+pad*2,h+pad*2);ctx.clip();}ctx.drawImage(bg,0,0,1536,1024);engine.draw(ctx,bg,zone,time,{active:enabled&&!document.hidden,showMask});if(bounds)for(const p of DFGBackgroundMotion.patches[zone]){ctx.strokeStyle='#fff2a8';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.setLineDash([9,5]);ctx.strokeRect(...p.box);}ctx.restore();}
Promise.all(Object.entries(maps).map(async([key,src])=>{const im=new Image();im.src=src;await im.decode();loaded[key]=im;})).then(()=>{list();sync();requestAnimationFrame(frame);}).catch(()=>{document.getElementById('motionStatus').textContent='Unable to load the scenery. Reload to try again.';});
</script><script src="adventure/ambient-pilot.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/ambient-pilot.js')?>"></script><script src="adventure/ambient-pilot-v2.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/ambient-pilot-v2.js')?>"></script><script src="adventure/riverside-section.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/riverside-section.js')?>"></script><script>for(const video of document.querySelectorAll('[data-ambient-preview-rate]')){const rate=Number(video.dataset.ambientPreviewRate);video.defaultPlaybackRate=rate;video.playbackRate=rate;video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata',()=>video.playbackRate=rate);}document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden)for(const video of document.querySelectorAll('[data-ambient-preview-rate]'))video.pause();});</script><script src="adventure/cedar-strength-study.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/cedar-strength-study.js')?>"></script><script src="adventure/cedar-sustained-study.js?v=<?=filemtime(__DIR__.'/cedar-sustained-study.js')?>"></script></body></html>
